  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x+2 & =0.5 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =-1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(-1.5)=-0.982\\,794\u2026\u2248-1.0\n$$\n\nSince $-1.0$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate solutions in the domain, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\pi +(-0.982\\,794\u2026)\u22482.2,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=2\\pi +(-0.982\\,794\u2026)\u22485.3.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=2.2$ and $x=5.3.$",
